<urn:atm:triage:finding/R7-QA1-FTQ-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "R7-QA1-FTQ-001" ;
  triage:title "tree() runs `cargo tree` through spawn_with_deadline(&mut cargo, None), which applies the " ;
  triage:description "tree() runs `cargo tree` through spawn_with_deadline(&mut cargo, None), which applies the shared 60 s SUBPROCESS_DEADLINE. The command has no --locked and no --offline, so it may touch the network to refresh the registry index and may wait on Cargo's package-cache or build-directory lock while a concurrent cargo process (for example the outer `cargo test --workspace`) holds it. On a cold or contended CI host the call can exceed 60 s and the runner kills it, so the test fails on some runs and passes on others depending on cache state and network speed. The test calls tree() 7 times (1 control, 1 workspace, 5 inverted queries), so it has 7 independent exposures to this window. The sprint already documents the same class of problem for builds: bin_path.rs gives cold release builds a 20 min deadline with a comment about 'Blocking waiting for file lock'. The cargo tree calls get no such treatment." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "timing_assertion" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-11-08T02:33:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:A1-R7 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-11-08T02:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/R7-QA1-FTQ-001/IPA-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/R7-QA1-FTQ-001/SDR-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

